; Raptor: Call of the Shadows - Amiga port
; Reference amiga.cfg (every value shown is the built-in default).
;
; Raptor creates amiga.cfg automatically on first run in the game directory
; (the drawer that also holds MP3/ and WAVE/). This file is only a
; reference/example - copy it to the game drawer as "amiga.cfg" if you want
; to start from it.
;
; Format: "key = value" lines. A line starting with ';' or '#' is a
; comment; blank lines are allowed; keys are case-insensitive; unknown
; keys are ignored; whitespace around '=' is optional.
;
; Volumes are integers in the range 0..127 (127 = loudest). When the
; in-game Options volumes are saved, this file is updated in place:
; comments, unknown keys, manual edits, key order, spacing and line endings
; are preserved and only the volume values are rewritten. Missing volume
; keys are appended.
;
; A legacy amiga.cfg that holds only audio volume keys is migrated once at
; load time: the missing volume keys and the JOYSTICK / 1-2-3 BUTTONS and
; JOYSTICK / CD32 blocks below are appended with the built-in defaults,
; keeping the original values, comments and line endings; the original is
; kept as amiga.cfg.bakN. A file that already holds controller keys or any
; other active key is never migrated automatically - copy the lines you want
; from this reference file (or from the matching section in README_AMIGA.md).
;
; The CD32=ON|OFF startup parameter (CLI "-cd32=on" or icon ToolType
; "CD32=ON") overrides the "cd32" key for the current session only; it is
; never written back to this file. An amiga.cfg written by an older build
; that contains an explicit "cd32_yellow = NONE" keeps that button disabled;
; remove the line (or set it to CANCEL) to get the new default.

; ==== AUDIO ====
; Raptor Amiga volumes (0..127, 127 = loud)
music_adlib = 127
music_mhi   = 127
music_wave  = 127
sfx_volume  = 127

; ==== JOYSTICK / 1-2-3 BUTTONS ====
; Amiga DB9 joystick on the second physical port.
; Active when cd32 = OFF. No separate enable setting is required.
; Buttons: 1 = pin 6, 2 = pin 9, 3 = pin 5.
; Action names (same set as the CD32 block below):
;   FIRE           - primary guns + selected secondary weapon
;   SPECIAL_SELECT - change (cycle) the secondary weapon
;   MEGA_BOMB      - launch a mega bomb
;   PAUSE          - pause the game
;   CANCEL         - cancel / back out
;   NONE           - button disabled
; The deprecated keys joy3_button1 / joy3_button2 / joy3_button3 are still
; accepted as aliases of joy_button1 / joy_button2 / joy_button3, so
; assignments from earlier builds keep working; a valid joy_buttonN wins over
; the joy3_buttonN alias for the same button. A leftover "joy3 = OFF" is
; ignored and no longer disables anything. If the button-3 line cannot be
; allocated, button 3 stays inactive, buttons 1/2 keep working and the
; startup log notes the limited mode.
joy_button1 = FIRE ; Button 1 (DB9 pin 6, fire line)
joy_button2 = SPECIAL_SELECT ; Button 2 (DB9 pin 9)
joy_button3 = MEGA_BOMB ; Button 3 (DB9 pin 5)

; ==== JOYSTICK / CD32 ====
; cd32 = OFF : shared joystick handling on port 1 (default)
; cd32 = ON  : CD32 pad on port 1 (lowlevel.library game controller mode)
; CD32=ON|OFF (CLI/ToolType) overrides this session only; NOJOY wins.
; Button assignments, one value per physical pad button:
;   FIRE           - primary guns + selected secondary weapon
;   SPECIAL_SELECT - change (cycle) the secondary weapon
;   MEGA_BOMB      - launch a mega bomb
;   PAUSE          - pause the game
;   CANCEL         - cancel / back out (default: yellow button)
;   NONE           - button disabled
; CANCEL equals the ESC key: in the shop it returns to the hangar, in the
; hangar it acts as the physical ESC key, and in game it asks
; "Abort Mission ?". It is assigned to the yellow button by default; set
; cd32_yellow = NONE to disable that button. The CD32 pad is selected with
; cd32 = ON below or, for one launch only, with the CD32=ON startup
; parameter (CLI -cd32=on / icon ToolType CD32=ON), which is never written
; back to this file. Joystick input is enabled by default, so an active
; CD32=ON ToolType is enough unless joystick input was disabled. A
; recommended, unambiguous icon configuration is the active pair, one per
; line and without parentheses: JOYSTICK=ON and CD32=ON; replace
; JOYSTICK=OFF with JOYSTICK=ON and remove (or parenthesize) an active
; NOJOY. "(CD32=ON)" is inactive, JOYSTICK=OFF / NOJOY disables controller
; polling, CD32=OFF only selects the joystick path (it does not disable
; input), and CD32=ON alone does not re-enable disabled input.
cd32 = OFF
cd32_red     = FIRE ; Red button
cd32_blue    = SPECIAL_SELECT ; Blue button
cd32_green   = MEGA_BOMB ; Green button
cd32_yellow  = CANCEL ; Yellow button
cd32_reverse = NONE ; Reverse button (left shoulder)
cd32_forward = NONE ; Forward button (right shoulder)
cd32_play    = PAUSE ; Play button (triangle)
